Why vendored: the workload build is JDK-only (no Maven or Gradle) and must work
offline. The core workload stays free of third-party code (docs/decisions.md
#5); only workload-libs.jar runs against these jars, named in its
manifest's Class-Path, not copied into it. `mage workloadLibsBuild` checks the
SHA-256s above before compiling.

Why this version: 4.2.20.Final is the newest release at least two weeks
old on the fetch date (4.2.21.Final was 3 days old). Netty 4.1 is not
tested: a 4.1 whose HttpObjectEncoder does not override write is not
seen.

To update: download the jars of the new version from Maven Central,
compare each SHA-1 with the published .sha1, replace the jars and license
files, and update the version, the hashes here and libsJars in
magefile_libs.go in the same commit.
